//RS /// Outermost Shared transactions run one at a time, process-wide. A body
//RS /// works on transaction-local copies taken at first touch and commit publishes
//RS /// them, so two transactions whose bodies overlapped would each publish a copy
//RS /// that misses the other's write. Holding the gate from begin to commit or
//RS /// rollback makes every transaction's copies current; contention waits and
//RS /// the body still runs once. Nested transactions join their parent and never
//RS /// take the gate again; the per-thread depth keeps an orphaned inner begin
//RS /// from waiting on its own thread.
//RS struct JetSharedTransactionGate;
